9:["Zambia’s economy depends on one metal. Why copper, and how is it taken out of rock?","fig:E_BLAST",[["Economy","Copper makes up most of Zambia’s exports; cobalt, gold, manganese and emeralds are also mined."],["Construction","Galvanised iron roofing sheets resist rusting because of a zinc coating."],["Environment","Mining and smelting can pollute rivers and air, as the 2025 Kafue River spill showed."]],[2,8,9,10],["What makes metals useful, and why are alloys used?","How does the reactivity series explain reactions and corrosion?","How are metals extracted from their ores?"]],
10:["Is the water from your borehole safe to drink? How would you know?","fig:E_TREAT",[["Health","Lusaka Water and Sewerage treats water with filtration and chlorine; shallow wells near pit latrines can carry nitrates and bacteria."],["Climate","Zambia’s droughts and floods are linked to a changing climate; carbon dioxide and methane levels are rising."],["Farming","Fertilisers raise maize yields but can cause eutrophication in rivers and dams."]],[7,9,10,11],["How is water tested and treated?","What pollutes the air, and how can pollution be reduced?","How do greenhouse gases and fertilisers affect the environment?"]],
